          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This way of associating each cow with a stick, such that no two cows are associated or mapped to the same stick is called a one-to-one mapping. This mapping can then be used to come up with a way to represent numbers, as shown in the table."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.27,
            0.166,
            0.728,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.27,
                0.166,
                0.728,
                0.4
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Number</td><td>Its representation (using sticks)</td></tr><tr><td>12345...</td><td>...</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.414,
            0.847,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? How will you use such sticks to answer the other two questions (Q2 and Q3)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.458,
            0.849,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Instead of objects, we could use a standard sequence of sounds or names. For example, we could use the sounds of the letters of any language. While counting, we could make a one-to-one mapping between the objects and the letters: that is, associate each object to be counted with a letter, following the letter-order. This mapping can then be used to come up with a way of verbally representing numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.569,
            0.847,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, we get the following number representation if we use English letters ‘a’ to ‘z’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
